<title>USA: U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Based on FOB Omaha basis</p>
<p>carlot prices of fabricated beef cuts and on industry yields as</p>
<p>of 1500 CDT, boxed beef values sharply higher on light demand</p>
<p>and offerings. Select and Choice rib, chuck and round cuts</p>
<p>higher, while loin cuts sharply higher. Beef trimmings generally</p>
<p>steady on very light demand. -- USDA Market News.</p>
<p> 228 Fab Lds  CH 1-3	CH 1-3	SE 1-3	SE 1-3</p>
<p>   9 50s Lds  550/700     700/850     550/700     700/850</p>
<p>31 Grd Lds ---------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Values =     107.46	108.18	100.97	101.18</p>
<p>		    2.23	  1.85	  1.38	  1.60</p>
<p>Rib	  171.35	171.17	158.28	157.00</p>
<p>Chuck	 73.70	 74.27	 74.55	 74.04</p>
<p>Round	 93.61	 93.61	 91.66	 91.66</p>
<p>Loin	 167.50	170.23	144.50	146.88</p>
<p>Brisket     65.52	 65.52	 65.75	 65.75</p>
<p>Shrt Plate  68.69	 68.60	 68.93	 68.75</p>
<p>Flank	 58.69	 58.69	 58.05	 58.05</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720))</p>
